    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa has a room-temperature yield strength of about 800 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa has a yield strength of about 330 MPa at 1273 K.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa exhibits approximately 40% strain at room temperature.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is to introduce 10–20 at.% Mo into TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A TiVNbTa alloy containing 10–20 at.% Mo can retain a single-phase BCC structure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12463061::web::013::comparison_of_the_temperature_and_strain"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-containing refractory multicomponent alloys retain yield strength relatively well at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence_ids",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12463061::web::013::comparison_of_the_temperature_and_strain"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition to TiVNbTa will increase lattice distortion and solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will favor edge-dislocation activity over screw-dislocation motion at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The shift toward edge-dislocation activity will stabilize the microstructure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo alters the alloy's internal energy landscape so that the Peierls barrier for edge-dislocation motion is relatively reduced.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa softening is associated with a temperature-sensitive screw-dislocation mechanism.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An edge-dislocation-dominated deformation regime will produce a high-temperature strength-retention plateau.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 10–20 at.% Mo will raise the 1273 K yield strength of TiVNbTa by approximately 30–50%, from about 330 MPa to about 430–500 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12463061::web::013::comparison_of_the_temperature_and_strain"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-modified alloy will maintain acceptable ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-modified alloy will better satisfy the requirements of a W-to-CuCrZr heat-transfer interlayer.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted improvement will persist at temperatures up to 1273 K under typical divertor loading conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12463061::web::013::comparison_of_the_temperature_and_strain",
        "PMC6397024::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Mo addition may destabilize the phase constitution or reduce room-temperature ductility.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
